                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fifth Meeting of the Working Group Participating in
                        the Washington Exploratory Talks on Security, July</hi> 22, 1948</p>
                <p>In further discussion of the memorandum on Item I, Mr. Stone expressed his
                    opinion that the concept of indirect aggression by the Soviet Union should be
                    more clearly presented. He also suggested altering the final sentence to stress
                    the mutual advantage of a security treaty to each participant, rather than the
                    joining of two distinct groups of Eastern and Western Hemisphere nations. The
                    group agreed that the paper before them could be referred to Mr. Lovett and the
                    Ambassadors for study and possible transmittal to their respective governments.
                    This paper is presumably the draft dated July 22, 1948, not printed, which
                    incorporated the revisions of the day’s meeting (840.20/7–2248). The memorandum
                    of the fifth meeting is not printed (840.20/7–2248).</p>
            </div>
